{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "SNG",
  "chapter": 2,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I am a rose of Sharon,\nA lily of the valleys.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As a lily among thorns,\nSo is my love among the daughters.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As the apple-tree among the trees of the wood,\nSo is my beloved among the sons.\nI sat down under his shadow with great delight,\nAnd his fruit was sweet to my taste.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He brought me to the banqueting-house,\nAnd his banner over me was love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Stay ye me with raisins, refresh me with apples;\nFor I am sick from love.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His left hand ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " under my head,\nAnd his right hand doth embrace me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I adjure you, O daughters of Jerusalem,\nBy the roes, or by the hinds of the field,\nThat ye stir not up, nor awake ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "my",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " love,\nUntil he please.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The voice of my beloved! behold, he cometh,\nLeaping upon the mountains,\nSkipping upon the hills.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is like a roe or a young hart:\nBehold, he standeth behind our wall;\nHe looketh in at the windows;\nHe glanceth through the lattice.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved spake, and said unto me,\nRise up, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For, lo, the winter is past;\nThe rain is over and gone;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The flowers appear on the earth;\nThe time of the singing ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of birds",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is come,\nAnd the voice of the turtle-dove is heard in our land;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The fig-tree ripeneth her green figs,\nAnd the vines are in blossom;\nThey give forth their fragrance.\nArise, my love, my fair one, and come away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O my dove, that art in the clefts of the rock,\nIn the covert of the steep place,\nLet me see thy countenance,\nLet me hear thy voice;\nFor sweet is thy voice, and thy countenance is comely.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Take us the foxes, the little foxes,\nThat spoil the vineyards;\nFor our vineyards are in blossom.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My beloved is mine, and I am his:\nHe feedeth ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his flock",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " among the lilies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "SNG.2.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:SNG.2.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Until the day be cool, and the shadows flee away,\nTurn, my beloved, and be thou like a roe or a young hart\nUpon the mountains of Bether.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
